          "entry": "When thick fog rolls in, Meterupa absorb the surrounding moisture and become faint and difficult to see. In this form, their paper bodies seem almost translucent as they silently drift through the mist. Travelers sometimes mistake Foggy Meterupa for wandering spirits when they catch brief glimpses of them between the trees."
        },
        {
          "generation": "Gen 2",
          "entry": "A thin mist continually surrounds it and thickens when it becomes frightened. Groups of Foggy Meterupa can blanket an area so thoroughly that travelers may unknowingly walk past the same landmark several times."
        }
      ]
    },
